  "notes": "HALF RESOLVED. The runtime closure is pinned: every wheel is named, sized and hashed from pypi.org, so the managed install fetches exactly what this repository claims and refuses anything else. The model, official voice and cloning artifacts are NOT recorded yet -- the machine that pinned the closure could not reach huggingface.co -- so the model half of the install refuses with a sentence naming tools/pin_pocket_models.py rather than fetching something nobody reviewed. Run `python tools/pin_pocket_models.py --model` on a machine that can reach the hub, with HF_TOKEN set and the Kyutai conditions accepted, to fill in the rest; the cloning half is gated and a closed gate leaves the public half resolved. Installing from a folder you filled yourself works either way, and records the digests of what it was given.",
