    "closure_notes": "The smallest tested inference-complete closure rather than everything pocket-tts declares. Upstream's project metadata also lists a server and a CLI; the import path Voice Chat uses needs neither, and section 23.1 says the closure is the smallest tested inference-complete one. torchao is deliberately absent: INT8 quantization is offered only once GATE P-5 has measured it on release hardware, and adding an optional accelerator before then would be pinning a dependency nothing has run. Torch is 2.6.0 rather than the 3.0.2 metadata's >=2.5.0 floor because 2.5.x has no cp313 Windows wheel and this manifest advertises Python 3.13; a floor is not a runtime identity, and a platform advertised without a wheel to satisfy it is a platform that fails at install time instead of at review time.",
